4,Godwari dialect — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/godwari_dialect,"The Godwari dialect, also known as Godwari, is a Rajasthani speech variety classified within the Indo-Aryan branch of the Indo-European language family, specifically under the Rājasthānī subgroup. [1] It serves as a sub-dialect of Marwari and is primarily spoken in the Godwar region of western Rajasthan, India, encompassing areas from Ahor Tehsil in Jalore district to Bali Tehsil in Pali ...",Godwari,Indo-European
